[6] signature collision (why the 4-model test cannot enforce `not a rename`)
========================================================================================
   pattern = tuple over (free, 2D-YM, M6, plaquette) of (undef | 0 | +):
   pat(m) = ('0', '+', '0', 'undef')
   M1 = sigma (charged-sector gap / area law)     pat = ('0', '+', '0', 'undef')   == pat(m)  COLLISION
   M2 = isolation radius (bottom atom <-> rest)   pat = ('0', '+', '0', 'undef')   == pat(m)  COLLISION
   M3 = HS rate (= 2*lambda_bot, control)         pat = ('0', '+', '0', 'undef')   == pat(m)  COLLISION
   m (reference, banned)                          pat = ('0', '+', '0', 'undef')   == pat(m)  COLLISION
   => every 4/4 passer has pattern (0,+,0,undef) == pat(m); the numeric value is NOT pinned.
   => M1 is numerically identical to m on 2D-YM (sigma == 3g^2/8, degenerate identity [T]).
   => the test is a (transfer-exists? , m>0?) bit test; pass-set = monotone relabelings of m.

========================================================================================
[7] extra rows needed to certify a non-rename
========================================================================================
   (5) massive free scalar, mass w : m=w>0, G''=2w>0, f1^2=1/(2w)>0, sigma=0, r_iso=w
   (6) free field + contact carrier : C(t)=0 (t>0), m=0  <-- kills every functional of one C
   consequence: sigma is NOT a function of m (m=w>0, sigma=0) -> sigma passes (5);
                but sigma is not a gap witness -> it witnesses a DIFFERENT sector.
   consequence: r_iso(w)=w and M3(w)=2w -> both collapse to m on any relativistic target.

========================================================================================
[8] audit of the existing U13 `pass` (c1/c3/c4)
========================================================================================
   U13 used C(t) = sum_j w_j e^{-E_j t} with c1 -> 0.375 = E_(1/2).
   that limit requires w_(1/2) > 0  =>  f1^2 > 0  in the fixture.
   the touchstone's 2D-YM row has f1^2 == 0 (trF^2 = H conserved => C is a contact term).
   => U13's c1/c3/c4 passes are carrier artefacts, not properties of 2D YM.

